# Build output
/build/
# Ignore dist/ CONTENTS (not the dir itself, so the `!` exceptions below can
# re-include the committed distlib consumer bundles — consumers pull them by
# path: the full library, the kernel-safe core profile, and the per-codec
# decode profiles (zlib/zstd/bzip2/xz/gzip/tar). A `/dist/` dir-exclude would
# make the `!file` re-includes impossible. `.deps` sidecars stay ignored — they
# are build metadata, not consumer bundles. Every re-included `.cyr` is gated by
# the dist-drift check in ci.yml; an untracked bundle would slip that gate
# silently (`git diff --quiet` on an untracked path always exits 0).
/dist/*
!dist/sankoch.cyr
!dist/sankoch-core.cyr
!dist/sankoch-zlib.cyr
!dist/sankoch-zstd.cyr
!dist/sankoch-bzip2.cyr
!dist/sankoch-xz.cyr
!dist/sankoch-gzip.cyr
!dist/sankoch-tar.cyr
!dist/sankoch-zip.cyr
!dist/sankoch-zipall.cyr
*.core

# Resolved deps — `cyrius deps` materialises lib/ from the toolchain pin, so
# nothing under it belongs in the tree. Through 2.7.8 this was `lib/*.cyr` plus
# a `!lib/k*.cyr` un-ignore, which tracked a keccak.cyr nothing references; the
# glob also missed subdirectories, so lib/unicode/ was committed by accident at
# c93cefe. 6.5.35's dep resolution stopped materialising either (neither is in
# [deps] stdlib), and both were removed at 2.7.9. Ignore the whole directory.
/lib/

# Lockfile policy: track when git-deps are present, otherwise omit.
# sankoch has zero git deps, so a lock pins nothing the `cyrius = "X.Y.Z"` pin
# in cyrius.cyml does not already pin. Through 6.4.69 no lock was generated at
# all; 6.5.16 locks the stdlib snapshot too, so one appears whether or not it
# says anything — 107 lines rewritten on every toolchain bump, for no
# reproducibility the manifest lacks. Ignored, which is the recipe this comment
# already described.
cyrius.lock

